# HARD RULE — health / legal content (public app)

FlareCare ships to the public. Getting health or legal content wrong can cause real harm and legal exposure.

**Use authoritative UK sources for health and legal information — never rely on general knowledge or invent guidance.**

## Before writing any health/legal product copy

1. Research named UK sources first (e.g. Crohn’s & Colitis UK, NHS, GOV.UK, Acas, EHRC, legislation.gov.uk).
2. Ground every claim in those pages. Prefer linking to the source in-app.
3. If you cannot find a source for a claim, **do not ship it** — ask Simon.

## Not allowed

- AI “general knowledge” as medical or legal guidance
- Freestyle triage (“call 999 if…”) unless quoted/paraphrased only as tightly as a named NHS/CCUK page supports, with a link
- Invented employment-rights advice beyond what Acas / GOV.UK / CCUK state
- Support guides, “What happens if…”, IBD at work, private topics, or similar without cited sources

## Disclaimers

Keep the legal/product stance accurate in **sourced copy**. Do **not** add a disclaimer footer to every new screen — FlareCare will use disclaimer wording **once, in one place later**. New screens: title + support + content only, unless Simon asks otherwise.

## Product stance

FlareCare helps people **understand and navigate**. It does **not** replace clinicians or lawyers.

Also recorded in `apps/mobile/DEV_NOTES.md` (top). Treat **sourcing** as non-negotiable from the **first message** of any session — not after a mistake.
